Anita Patel: quick ping — after upgrading node-sdk to v7.0 we're seeing streaming sessions drop whenever we rotate access tokens mid-stream. repro below, anyone seen this?

Anita Patel: repro (simple):
```js
const s = client.stream.chat({model: 'redwood-3b'});
await s.open();
// rotate token externally here
s.on('data', d => console.log(d));
// connection drops with AuthExpiredError after ~30s
```

Kevin Liu: yep ran into this yesterday. breaking change in 7.0: the client no longer automatically re-auths an existing socket on token refresh — it emits an AuthExpiredError and closes by default.

Maia Chen: iirc there's a new auth hook you can pass as an option to keep the socket alive. something like `authRefresh` that returns a promise with new token.

Oliver Park: short term workaround for node: intercept AuthExpiredError and call `client.stream(...)` again with same session id? but that causes duplication of partial events. not great.

Anita Patel: thanks — any recommended migration pattern to avoid dupes? we're doing live-collab so duplicates are bad.

Kevin Liu: recommended pattern from eng-runtime: provide a token provider instead of a static token. example: 
```js
const provider = async () => {
  if (token.isExpired()) await rotate();
  return token.value;
};
const s = client.stream.chat({ model: 'redwood-3b', authProvider: provider, resume_on_token_refresh: true });
```
This is new in 7.x; `resume_on_token_refresh` flips the old behavior and tries to continue the stream where possible.

Maia Chen: for python clients it's similar but uses an async callback: `auth_callback=auth_fn` on `ClientStream` and there's `resume_on_token_refresh=True` too. watch out: the parameter name changed from `on_token_refresh` -> `auth_callback` (breaking).

Anita Patel: oh nice — where's the docs? I searched migration guide but didn't find resume flag.

Kevin Liu: docs PR is landing today on dev portal; for now internal note: runtime will only resume if KV cache is enabled and the model supports resumption (most decoder-only models do; chat-formatted sequences sometimes need extra handling). If resumption fails, the stream will still close — handle AuthExpiredError fallback.

Oliver Park: another gotcha: retry/backoff signatures changed. `maxRetries` moved from top-level client opts into `retryPolicy: { maxRetries: 3, jitter: true }`. If you depended on implicit retries on stream open, you need to set it explicitly now.

Anita Patel: thanks — i'll try authProvider + resume flag and add explicit retryPolicy. will report back if duplicates still happen.

devex-bot: heads-up: created internal issue DEVEX-4221 to track node streaming token-rotation docs + sample snippet.

Maia Chen: ping me if you need a quick pairing session — i can replicate locally with the infra token rotation simulator. :thumbsup:

Anita Patel: appreciated! will loop you in if needed :)
